## Workflow State Machine

> Based on [LangGraph State Machine](https://www.langchain.com/langgraph) explicit state definition

**Core Concept**: State machine is **advisory guidance** not **mandatory constraint**. Provides audit, interrupt recovery, visualization, but Agent retains full autonomy.

### Design Philosophy: Advisory Mode

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|  State Machine = Navigation Map, Not Rails                   |
|  - Provides recommended path, allows detours when needed     |
|  - Records actual path for audit and learning                |
|  - Abnormal situations can trigger "escape hatch"            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
```

**When to deviate from state machine:**
- Agent confidence conflicts with preset path
- More efficient execution path discovered
- User explicitly requests skip
- External environment changed (e.g., code already modified)

### State Machine Definition

```yaml
name: mission-runner-pir
version: "2.0"

states:
  init:
    description: "Initialize planning files"
    next: read_before_decide

  read_before_decide:
    description: "Read plan files, anchor to goal"
    next: confidence_check

  confidence_check:
    description: "Evaluate current task confidence"
    transitions:
      high: execute           # >= 4
      medium: execute         # 3-4 (with recording)
      low: ask_user           # < 3

  ask_user:
    description: "Wait for user clarification"
    next: confidence_check    # Re-evaluate after clarification

  execute:
    description: "Execute current task"
    next: validate

  validate:
    description: "Validate execution results"
    transitions:
      pass: checkpoint
      fail: self_reflection

  self_reflection:
    description: "Analyze failure cause"
    transitions:
      simple_error: execute   # Retry immediately
      medium_error: checkpoint # Record, next iteration
      complex_error: ask_user  # Need user clarification

  checkpoint:
    description: "Update progress, check completion"
    transitions:
      complete: done
      continue: read_before_decide
      max_iterations: report

  done:
    description: "Task complete"
    output: "<promise>Mission Accomplished</promise>"

  report:
    description: "Report partial completion"
    output: "Remaining tasks + suggestions"
```

### State Machine Visualization

```
                    +--------------------------------------------------+
                    |                                                  |
                    v                                                  |
              +----------+                                            |
              |   init   |                                            |
              +----+-----+                                            |
                   |                                                  |
                   v                                                  |
         +-------------------+                                       |
         | read_before_decide|<--------------------------------------+
         +---------+---------+                                       |
                   |                                                  |
                   v                                                  |
          +----------------+     low      +-----------+              |
          |confidence_check|------------>|  ask_user |              |
          +--------+-------+              +-----+-----+              |
                   | high/medium                |                    |
                   v                            | (clarified)        |
              +---------+<---------------------+                    |
              | execute |                                            |
              +----+----+                                            |
                   |              +-----------------+                |
                   v              | self_reflection |                |
              +----------+  fail  +--------+--------+                |
              | validate |---------------->|                         |
              +----+-----+                 | simple_error            |
                   | pass                  +----------->|            |
                   v                                    |            |
             +------------+<--------(medium)------------+            |
             | checkpoint |                                          |
             +------+-----+                                          |
                    |                                                |
           +--------+--------+                                      |
           |        |        |                                      |
           v        v        v                                      |
       +------+ +--------+ +--------+                               |
       | done | | report | |continue|-------------------------------+
       +------+ +--------+ +--------+
```

### State Persistence

```json
// _planning/workflow_state.json
{
  "current_state": "execute",
  "iteration": 2,
  "retry_count": 0,
  "phase": "implementation",
  "task_index": 3,
  "confidence_scores": {
    "understanding": 5,
    "certainty": 4,
    "dependencies": 4,
    "risk": 4
  },
  "timestamp": "2024-01-15T15:30:00Z"
}
```

### State Machine Usage Rules (Advisory)

```
1. [Advised] Update workflow_state.json on state transition - for interrupt recovery
2. [Advised] Interrupt recovery: Read workflow_state.json, continue from current_state
3. [Advised] Audit log: Record state changes to mission_notes.md Progress Log
4. [Optional] Visualization: State machine diagram can embed in task reports
5. [Allowed] When deviating, record reason to mission_notes.md Decisions Made
```

### Escape Hatch Mechanism

When state machine "stuck" or inapplicable, trigger escape hatch:

```yaml
escape_hatch:
  triggers:
    - agent_confidence < 0.3          # Agent confidence too low
    - iteration_count > max_iterations # Too many iterations
    - user_command: "free_form"        # User intervention
    - path_conflict: true              # Recommended path conflicts with reality

  actions:
    fallback_to_free_form:
      description: "Switch to free execution mode, keep mission_plan.md as goal reference"
      preserve:
        - mission_plan.md              # Keep goal
        - mission_notes.md             # Keep records
      suspend:
        - workflow_state.json          # Pause state tracking

    record_deviation:
      description: "Record deviation reason, continue execution"
      append_to: mission_notes.md
      section: "Deviations & Reasons"
```

**After triggering escape hatch:**
1. Agent regains full autonomy, no longer bound by state machine
2. Still keeps mission_plan.md as goal reference (not mandatory)
3. After task completion, record "free-form mode" path for future learning

